name iso-639-3-macrolanguages
# ISO 639-3's macrolanguage mappings: each row says of an individual language its macrolanguage and its status. SIL's
# iso639-3_macrolanguages_table_definition.txt:
#   "M_Id      char(3) NOT NULL,   -- The identifier for a macrolanguage"
#   "I_Id      char(3) NOT NULL,   -- The identifier for an individual language that is a member of the macrolanguage"
#   "I_Status  char(1) NOT NULL)   -- A (active) or R (retired) indicating the status of the individual code element"
# The row is about the individual language (I_Id); what it says of it is that it is a member of the macrolanguage
# M_Id names, and the status of its code element, a value of the table's own list (A, R).
match iso-639-3-macrolanguages.tab
# The table does not name who publishes it; the pages kept beside it in sil/ are signed "Copyright © 2026 SIL Global".
witness SIL Global

tier row by \n
header
tier field by \t

thing row I_Id
content I_Id M_Id I_Status
relation "a member of the macrolanguage" M_Id
value - I_Status
attest row M_Id I_Status
